/* ===== RELIGIOUS STUDIES · MONGOLIAN (faith pack, July 2026) =====
   PRIMARILY FOR MONGOLIAN PEOPLE to learn about Jesus — Mongolian is the
   primary language everywhere (titles, story text, explanations), with
   English the quiet second line. Mirrors faith/ne.js: the same two stories,
   the same 10+10 big-moment sections, the same shared scene art.
   Deliberately Christian (the secular-content rule does NOT apply in faith
   mode). Content register: rich storytelling for the un-churched reader —
   every person, place and church-word introduced in-story on first use
   (Adam & Eve, Eden, Noah, Abraham, sacrifice, the prophets, exile,
   disciples, Mary Magdalene). Paraphrase only — no Bible-translation text
   is copied; references name the passages retold.
   VOCABULARY DECISION — the word for God: Mongolian has a real split.
   Бурхан also means Buddha, so the Bible Society of Mongolia coined
   Ертөнцийн Эзэн (Lord of the universe) to avoid the association, while
   Тэнгэр carries shamanist weight. This pack uses БУРХАН, because the
   Ариун Библи — the translation most Mongolian churches actually use —
   uses it, and it is what Mongolian Christians say. Verified against the
   Ариун Библи 2013 text of John 3:16 (Бурхан … цорын ганц Хүүгээ …
   итгэдэг бүхэн … мөнх амь).
   Vocabulary: Бурхан (God), Эзэн / Их Эзэн (Lord), Есүс (Jesus), Хүү
   (Son), нүгэл (sin), итгэх / итгэл (believe / faith), хайр (love),
   аврах / аврал (save / salvation), Аврагч (Rescuer), сайн мэдээ
   (gospel), загалмай (cross), Ариун Сүнс (Holy Spirit), амлалт
   (promise), гэрээ (covenant), нөхөрлөл (fellowship), эш үзүүлэгч
   (prophet), шавь (disciple), тахил (sacrifice), цөллөг (exile),
   хаанчлал (kingdom), тэнгэр (heaven), тэнгэр элч (angel), сүм
   (temple), баптисм (baptism), залбирах (pray), амилах (rise),
   мөнх амь (eternal life).
   Register: Mongolian church usage is PLAIN — there is no royal-verb
   system like Khmer or Lao. Respect rides on word choice (Их Эзэн,
   Ариун) and on the polite та, not on special verbs; the Ариун Библи
   uses ordinary past forms for God (хайрласан, өгсөн), and so does this
   pack. Romanization follows the Mongolian course scheme in lang/mn.js
   (ASCII word roms: ө→o, ү→u — Burkhan, Yesus, monkh; х=kh, ц=ts,
   ч=ch, ш=sh, ж=j, з=z, е=ye, ё=yo, ю=yu, я=ya; long vowels doubled;
   the soft sign ь is not written). Mongolian uses WESTERN NUMERALS, so
   this pack carries no digits[] array. Native strings must avoid the
   chars ' " < > \ (they ride inline onclick handlers — use dashes for
   speech).
   IMPORTANT: keep paras[i][0] AND note[0] byte-stable once audio exists —
   clips in audio-mnf/ are hashed from these exact strings. Regenerate with
     osascript -l JavaScript extract_audio_strings.js mnf
     python3 generate_audio.py --lang mnf
   Scene art is shared with the Nepali pack (language-independent scene
   emblems — scenes and symbols only, no depictions of God or of Jesus'
   face). */
